<main id="main">
<section class="phero"><div class="phero-bg"><img src="/assets/img/photos/storm-clouds.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/storm-clouds-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/storm-clouds.webp 1024w" sizes="100vw" width="1024" height="683" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" data-parallax="0.18"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li><a href="/service-locations/">Locations</a></li><li aria-current="page">Frederick</li></ol></nav><p class="kicker">Capital Region · Frederick County</p><h1>Frederick Insurance Appraiser for Hail, Roof and Historic Claims</h1><p class="lede">Frederick mixes an 18th- and 19th-century downtown with fast-growing subdivisions that see their share of hail and wind. Our role as insurance appraiser in Frederick, MD is to price both kinds of building fairly.</p><div class="btns"><a class="btn brass" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn ghost-l" href="/start-a-claim-review/">Request a free review</a></div><dl class="ph-facts"><div><dt>County</dt><dd>Frederick County</dd></div><div><dt>Region</dt><dd>Capital Region</dd></div><div><dt>Inspections</dt><dd>On site</dd></div></dl></div></section><div class="wrap two-col"><article class="prose"><div class="localcard"><div><h2 class="lc-h">Local claim risks</h2><ul class="chips"><li>Hail</li><li>Straight-line wind</li><li>Creek flooding</li><li>Heavy snow</li><li>Ice dams</li></ul></div><div><h2 class="lc-h">Storms on record</h2><ul class="dots"><li>Tropical Storm Agnes, 1972</li><li>February 2010 blizzards</li><li>June 2012 derecho</li></ul></div><div class="full"><h2 class="lc-h">Housing mix</h2><p>Brick and stone rowhouses in the downtown historic district, with newer vinyl-sided subdivisions and townhouse communities spreading across Frederick County.</p><p class="hoods"><b>Neighborhoods &amp; nearby:</b> Downtown Frederick, Ballenger Creek, Urbana, Walkersville, Middletown, New Market, Thurmont</p></div></div><h2>Two Fredericks, two kinds of claim</h2>
<p>Frederick is the county seat and the largest city in Frederick County, and it carries two very different building stocks. The downtown historic district along Market and Patrick Streets is full of 18th- and 19th-century brick and stone buildings. Around it, subdivisions in Urbana, Ballenger Creek, New Market and Walkersville were mostly built in recent decades. An insurance appraiser in Frederick, MD needs to price an old slate roof on a downtown rowhouse just as carefully as hail on a vinyl-sided colonial.</p>
<h2>Hail season and newer subdivisions</h2>
<p>Severe thunderstorms with hail are most common in Maryland’s central and western counties in spring and summer, and Frederick County lies right in that belt. Newer homes typically have architectural shingles, vinyl siding and aluminum gutters, all of which show hail differently. Typical disagreements include:</p>
<ul>
<li>Roof slopes left off when hits are counted on only the most visible side</li>
<li>Siding repairs on one elevation when replacement panels can’t be matched</li>
<li>Gutters, downspouts, window wraps and soft metals dismissed as cosmetic</li>
<li>Roof measurements that undercount squares, pitch or waste</li>
</ul>
<p>Our <a href="/appraisal-calculators/roof-square-pitch-calculator/">roof square and pitch calculator</a> lets you sanity-check the measurements on your carrier’s estimate.</p>
<h2>Downtown buildings and the historic district</h2>
<p>Older downtown buildings use plaster, heavy timber framing, original windows and masonry that modern pricing tools often skip. Exterior work in the historic district may require review, which can add time and cost. Fire and water losses in attached buildings also raise the same party-wall questions found in Baltimore.</p>
<h2>Storms remembered locally</h2>
<p>Tropical Storm Agnes in June 1972 brought serious flooding to the Monocacy River. Today flash flooding in stream valleys is still a risk after slow-moving storms, and flood remains a separate coverage. More recently, the February 2010 blizzards loaded roofs across the county, and the June 2012 derecho knocked down trees and power lines widely. Wind and snow claims are often where scope and pricing disputes surface.</p>
<h2>Communities around Frederick we serve</h2>
<p>We inspect in downtown Frederick and in Ballenger Creek, Urbana, Walkersville, Middletown, New Market and Thurmont. Commercial and HOA properties along the I-270 and I-70 corridors raise their own questions about shared roofs and master policies.</p>
<p>Because so many subdivisions in the county were built at the same time with the same materials, a single hailstorm can damage hundreds of similar roofs. Carriers sometimes apply a standard approach to every claim in a neighborhood, which can miss differences in roof age, layers, pitch and accessories from one house to the next.</p>
<h2>Advice before you accept a Frederick estimate</h2>
<p>After hail, photograph soft metals such as gutters, vents and AC fins, since they record impacts clearly. Keep the date and time of the storm. If the carrier offers a partial roof repair, ask for the reasoning in writing, and get a roofer’s view on whether a repair is possible.</p>
<p>Maryland Insurance Appraiser can compare the carrier’s scope with your property and represent you through appraisal if the difference is significant.</p><h2>Services for Frederick property owners</h2><p>Every service is available in Frederick and the rest of Frederick County, including:</p><ul class="cols2"><li><a href="/property-claim-services/appraisal-demand-representation/">Appraisal Demand Representation</a></li><li><a href="/property-claim-services/home-insurance-appraisal/">Home Insurance Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/property-claim-services/commercial-hoa-appraisal/">Commercial &amp; HOA Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/property-claim-services/roof-hail-damage-appraisal/">Roof &amp; Hail Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/property-claim-services/windstorm-tornado-appraisal/">Windstorm &amp; Tornado Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/property-claim-services/hurricane-noreaster-appraisal/">Hurricane &amp; Nor’easter Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/property-claim-services/water-damage-appraisal/">Water Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/property-claim-services/fire-smoke-damage-appraisal/">Fire &amp; Smoke Damage Appraisal</a></li></ul>
<h2>Frederick claim questions</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>How do I prove hail hit my Frederick roof if I can’t get up there?<span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="a"><p>Soft metals like gutters, downspouts, vents and AC fins often show dents that are visible from the ground. Photograph those, keep the storm date, and ask a roofer or appraiser to inspect the shingles directly.</p></div></details><details><summary>Does historic district review affect what my insurer pays?<span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="a"><p>It can affect the cost of repair. If the work must meet historic requirements, check whether your policy includes ordinance or law coverage, which may pay for some code-driven costs. The amount owed under that coverage can be part of an appraisal.</p></div></details></div><h2>Nearby service areas</h2><div class="rel"><a href="/service-locations/hagerstown/"><small>Nearby</small><span>Hagerstown</span><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a><a href="/service-locations/rockville/"><small>Nearby</small><span>Rockville</span><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a><a href="/service-locations/ellicott-city/"><small>Nearby</small><span>Ellicott City</span><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a></div></article><aside class="side"><div class="side-in"><div class="box box-call"><h2 class="box-h">Talk to an appraiser</h2><p>A free first conversation about your estimate — and a straight answer on whether appraisal fits.</p><a class="box-tel" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg>(844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn brass block" href="/start-a-claim-review/">Send claim details</a><small>Mon–Fri, 8am–6pm ET</small></div><div class="box"><h2 class="box-h">Maryland locations</h2><ul class="box-list"><li><a href="/service-locations/baltimore/">Baltimore<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M9 18l6-6-6-6"/></svg></a></li><li><a href="/service-locations/towson/">Towson<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M9 18l6-6-6-6"/></svg></a></li><li><a href="/service-locations/ellicott-city/">Ellicott City<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M9 18l6-6-6-6"/></svg></a></li><li><a href="/service-locations/annapolis/">Annapolis<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M9 18l6-6-6-6"/></svg></a></li><li><a href="/service-locations/frederick/" aria-current="page">Frederick<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M9 18l6-6-6-6"/></svg